  "description": "Video capture SDK for .NET (C#, VB.NET, WinForms, WPF, console): TVideoGrabber is a video capture, recording, streaming and playback component for Windows 10/11. Captures webcams, USB/HDMI/PCIe capture devices and the desktop screen; connects to ONVIF, RTSP, RTMP and HTTP IP cameras (with the Datastead RTSP/RTMP/HTTP/ONVIF DirectShow source filter); records to MP4, MKV, AVI, WMV with the built-in Microsoft Media Foundation and GPU encoders (H.264, AV1, AAC); with the Datastead Multipurpose DirectShow Encoder, records to MOV, MPEG-TS, WebM and the other FFmpeg formats with H.264/HEVC/AV1 hardware encoding (NVIDIA NVENC, Intel QuickSync, AMD AMF) and streams to RTSP, RTMP, SRT, UDP, HLS; plays media files up to 8K with GPU decoding, HDR to SDR conversion and frame-accurate seeking; frame capture, text and image overlays, picture-in-picture, mixing of several sources, motion detection, 360-degree video, AES encryption. Multiple instances per application. Evaluation version: watermark on the video, recordings without watermark (native format, audio only) limited to 5 minutes per application run; a license is required for deployment (https://www.datastead.com/purchase/), fully functional 30-day trial on request (sales@datastead.com).",
